{"name":"Mediaeval Forest","hex":"#007e6b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mediaeval","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of medieval."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of medieval."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediaeval"},{"term":"forest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dense uncultivated tract of trees and undergrowth, larger than woods.","Any dense collection or amount."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover an area with trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Middle Ages","blocks":[{"text":"In the history of Europe, the Middle Ages or medieval period lasted approximately from the 5th to late 15th centuries, comparable with the post-classical period of global history. The medieval period is the middle epoch of the three traditional divisions of Western history: classical antiquity, the medieval period, and the modern period. The medieval period is itself subdivided into the Early, High, and Late Middle Ages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Canterbury_Cathedral%2C_window_nXV_detail_%2846220634195%29.jpg/330px-Canterbury_Cathedral%2C_window_nXV_detail_%2846220634195%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Middle_Ages","wikidata":"Q12554"},{"title":"Forest","blocks":[{"text":"A forest is an ecosystem characterized by a dense community of trees. Hundreds of definitions of forest are used throughout the world, incorporating factors such as tree density, tree height, land use, legal standing, and ecological function. The United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) defines a forest as, \"Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban use.\" Using this definition, Global Forest Resources Assessment 2025 found that forests covered 4.14 billion hectares, or approximately 31 percent of the world's land area in 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/330px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest","wikidata":"Q4421"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Venice_city_scenes_-_in_St._Mark%27s_square_-_St_Mark%27s_Basilica_%2811002237996%29.jpg/500px-Venice_city_scenes_-_in_St._Mark%27s_square_-_St_Mark%27s_Basilica_%2811002237996%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Venice_city_scenes_-_in_St._Mark%27s_square_-_St_Mark%27s_Basilica_%2811002237996%29.jpg/1280px-Venice_city_scenes_-_in_St._Mark%27s_square_-_St_Mark%27s_Basilica_%2811002237996%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Venice_city_scenes_-_in_St._Mark%27s_square_-_St_Mark%27s_Basilica_%2811002237996%29.jpg/500px-Venice_city_scenes_-_in_St._Mark%27s_square_-_St_Mark%27s_Basilica_%2811002237996%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A late Roman sculpture depicting the four Tetrarchs, now in Venice, Italy[21]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVenice_city_scenes_-_in_St._Mark's_square_-_St_Mark's_Basilica_(11002237996).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Europe_and_the_Near_East_at_476_AD.png/500px-Europe_and_the_Near_East_at_476_AD.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Europe_and_the_Ne